With that it works fine for me.

Yes, it is audio-video sync that is more difficult to do in a good way if the audio jumps in pts. I like video to be as smooth as possible.
mpv is not that good at handling sync during speed change but it is even more difficult if audio pts jumps around.
What type of video and parameters do you use when you can hear clicks?
I have not succeeded to hear them.
One alternative to adding silence is to repeat last audio from filter.
A very simple way could be to replace 
`mp_aframe_set_silence(new, out_samples, add);`
with:
```
                   int to = out_samples;
                    while (add > out_samples) {
                        mp_aframe_copy_samples(new, to, out, 0, out_samples);
                        add -= out_samples;
                        to += out_samples;
                    }
                    if (add > 0) {
                        mp_aframe_copy_samples(new, to, out, 0, add);
                    }
```
